lines=['# Wave 02-06 — semantic design and CSS acceptance','',f"Recommended outcome: **{summary.get('complete',0)} complete, {summary.get('partial',0)} partial** across the 15 assigned obligations. No shared acceptance count or checkbox changed.",'',f"Reviewed modified `dev` checkout at `{e['head']}`; capture timestamp `{e['capturedAt']}`. Exact requirements, source/test references, hashes, performed checks and limits are in [results.json](results.json) and [evidence.json](evidence.json). These are acceptance obligations, not a request for 15 new unit tests.",'','## Evidence and new work','', 'Reused FA-01–04 and parallel-06/08/10 reconciliation; did not repeat accepted inventories or passed suites. The source list for CSS and geometry review comes from FA-02, so no new repository inventory was generated. 167 selected inputs were initially hashed; five additional explicitly read inputs were appended. No input was missing. Token source/generator/tests, reviewed container/overlay/layout implementations and docs theme inputs match saved bytes. The shared acceptance checklist/ledger changed, as expected. TextArea.tsx and TextArea.module.css changed concurrently during coordinator BUG-0009 work; the new decorated multiline implementation is observed source only. No old build/guard/unit result is attributed to those changes. The three concurrently repaired picker implementations are outside this report’s behavioral claims.','', 'The only new executable evidence is a bounded selected-input/source receipt and an in-memory PostCSS/CSS Modules nesting probe. The probe passed parent/child class-scoping assertions and preserves native & syntax; it wrote no shared output and ran on local Node 26.5.0. That is compiler behavior, not the required Node 22/24 production matrix or browser support. [styling-mappings.json](styling-mappings.json) supplies a newly reconciled five-field historical wrapper migration table. [successor-deliverables.md](successor-deliverables.md) supplies concrete emphasis guidance, scale decisions, state applicability matrix, containment map, RTL reproduction, nesting support/adoption requirements, fluid sizing assessment and publication/preference selections. Drafts are reviewable but not landed source changes.','', 'FA-04’s original all-in-one command remained failed; only its corrected calendar rerun and unchanged passing cases were reconciled. Token/CSS tests and selected unchanged units retain their recorded aggregate local evidence. The passed package audit is evidence for its saved distributable, not current modified TextArea/pickers. Old container-query reports explicitly prepared native cases without executing them; inspecting their assertions does not upgrade them to passed geometry evidence. No current native/browser/OS/device/AT, remote CI, owner/legal sign-off or release result is claimed.','', '## Per-leaf results','']
